            "option_id": "b",
            "truth": "correct",
            "derivation": "Normalize 0.3333 to 33.33, add the captured 0.003 correction to 5.771, divide the root by 10 and multiply by 6: 3.4644. The second main entry gives 3.464; both final reports round to 3.464. The second route needs only the main entry instead of the first route's main entry, correction, scale and final multiplication.",
            "misconception": null
          },
          {
            "option_id": "c",
            "truth": "incorrect",
            "derivation": "After correctly obtaining 5.774, divide the root by 100 instead of 10, then multiply by 6: 5.774/100*6=0.34644, rounding to 0.346. Root scaling must use the square root of the argument's scale factor.",
